 # CHANGELOG — pickem
 
 Format: newest entry first. One entry per work session that touches code or
 docs; note the task(s), the commit range if known, and what changed.
 
+## 2026-10-09 — Remove the pick-history section from the player page
+
+Owner's call: it "doesn't serve any purpose and it's just large and noisy."
+Removed the SPA section only — the API contract with the ai-server
+`pickem-analysis` skill is untouched.
+
+- **`frontend/src/pages/Player.tsx`** — dropped the "Pick history" `<section>`,
+  the `PickHistory` import, and the now-unused `history` destructuring.
+  Module docstring's claim that the stats "and the pick history are computed
+  together server-side and must agree" no longer describes a section that
+  exists, so it was rewritten.
+- **`frontend/src/components/PickHistory.tsx`** — deleted (confirmed via
+  `grep -rn PickHistory frontend/src` that nothing else imported it).
+- **`frontend/src/api.ts`** — kept `PickHistoryRow` and `PlayerDetail.history`
+  (the SPA no longer renders them, but `GET /api/players/{id}` still returns
+  `history` for the `pickem-analysis` skill, a cross-repo consumer); added a
+  comment on `history` explaining why it stays. `app/api.py` /
+  `_pick_history` untouched, per that two-repo contract.
+- **`frontend/src/theme.css`** — removed the pick-history-only rules
+  (`table.board td .spread`, `table.board tr.group-row th`, `.res`,
+  `.res--correct`, `.res--incorrect`, `.res--missing`) after confirming by
+  grep that nothing else in `frontend/src` references them. Left `.muted`
+  and `.group-note` in place — both are shared with `WeekReview.tsx` /
+  `Compare.tsx` — and renamed the section comment from "pick history" to
+  "shared table bits" since that's all that's left in it.
+
+Gate: `npm run lint && npm run build` clean (Player's bundle shrank from
+11.45 kB to 8.86 kB; module count 618 → 617). `.venv/bin/pytest -q`
+unaffected (546 passed, 7 deselected) since no backend code changed.
+
+## 2026-10-09 — Team rows keyed by (sport, team), not the bare abbreviation
+
+Confirmed on production data: `HOU` is both the NFL Texans and the NCAAF
+Cougars, and `app/scoring/stats.py` aggregated picked teams into `teams`
+dicts keyed on the raw CBS abbreviation, so the player page's "Teams backed
+most" table (`top_teams`) and the league `/analytics` "most trusted teams"
+table (`most_trusted`) silently merged the two teams' picks into one row
+(188 league-wide picks sit on `HOU`).
+
+- **`app/scoring/stats.py`** — `player_stats`'s `top_teams` and
+  `league_analytics`'s `most_trusted` now key their internal `teams` dicts
+  on `(sport, team)` instead of the bare team string, and each row carries
+  a new `sport` field. Tie-break keys extended with `sport` so both stay
+  deterministic: `top_teams` is `(-picks, -correct, team, sport)`;
+  `most_trusted` is `(-pick_rate, -picks, team, sport)`. Both caps
+  (`_TOP_TEAMS`, `_TRUSTED_TEAMS`) now count (sport, team) pairs, so e.g.
+  HOU-NFL and HOU-NCAAF occupy two of the five/ten slots. Docstrings
+  (module-level and both functions') updated to explain the keying and why
+  (CBS abbreviations are only unique per sport).
+- **`tests/test_stats.py`** — updated every assertion pinning `top_teams`/
+  `most_trusted` row shape or contents to include `sport`; added
+  `test_the_same_abbreviation_in_two_sports_is_two_team_rows`, a fixture
+  where the same abbreviation (`HOU`) appears in an NCAAF game and an NFL
+  game and one player picks it in both, asserting two separate rows (one
+  per sport) whose `picks` sum to the player's total picks on that
+  abbreviation, plus the parallel `most_trusted` assertion.
+- **`frontend/src/api.ts`** — `TopTeam` and `TrustedTeam` gained a
+  `sport: string` field (with doc comments explaining the collision).
+- **`frontend/src/pages/Player.tsx`** / **`Analytics.tsx`** — `TEAM_COLUMNS`
+  / `TRUSTED_COLUMNS` gained a "Sport" column right after the team name;
+  `rowKey` on both `PrizeTable` calls changed from `row.team` to
+  `` `${row.sport}-${row.team}` `` — the bare team name is no longer a
+  unique React key once two sports can share an abbreviation.
+
+Full suite: 546 passed, 7 deselected (`live`). Frontend: `npm run lint` and
+`npm run build` both clean.
+
